# What `railway up` must never upload, spelled out rather than left to
# .gitignore: the local database, the survey frames and any .env are named here
# because the CLI may not read the nested .gitignore that keeps
# packages/server/data out.
.git/
.env*
!.env.example
**/node_modules/
packages/server/data/
**/survey-out/

# The rest, about 20 MB the build never reads. Anchored with a leading slash:
# like .gitignore, a bare "images/" matches a folder of that name at any depth,
# and so dropped packages/server/src/images (the first deploy could not boot).
/.superpowers/
/.claude/
/docs/
/images/
/legacy/
/research/
/e2e/test-results/
